  "limitations": [
    "The ranking is a stated rubric, not a fitted model. No labelled set of correct target rankings exists to fit against.",
    "`druggable_class` and `essential_class` are read from a hand-written keyword table against UniProt annotations on homologs. A term the table does not list reads as 'not druggable' rather than as 'not in my vocabulary'.",
    "`structures_in_family` is a count of deposited structures and is therefore a record of research attention as much as of tractability. It carries the smallest weight for that reason and is capped at 50.",
    "Six-frame calling misses frameshifted products: SARS-CoV-2's replicase is one 7,096-residue polyprotein and is ranked here as two fragments, because no ORF caller reading stop codons can see a ribosomal frameshift.",
    "These are whole ORFs. A polyprotein is one row here and is cut into its mature chains by the stage after this one, so the scores below are not the per-chain scores the shortlist is drawn from."
  ],
